This implementation first retrieves the plan and sqitch objects from the engine instance. It then retrieves the indexes of the changes in the plan, and uses these indexes to call the C<_verify_changes> method. This method loops over the changes between the from and to indexes, calling the C<verify_change> method for each change. If any errors occur, the method returns false. Otherwise, it returns true.

The C<verify_change> method is responsible for verifying each individual change. It first emits a message indicating the change being verified, and then runs the verify script for the change. If the verify script fails, the method returns false. Otherwise, it returns true.

The C<_from_idx> and C<_to_idx> methods are used to find the indexes of the changes in the plan. These methods take the from and to identifiers as input, and return the indexes of the corresponding changes. If no from identifier is provided, the method returns the index of the first change in the plan. If no to identifier is provided, the method returns the index of the last change in the plan.

The C<_verify_changes> method is responsible for verifying the changes between the from and to indexes. It first calls the C<_trim_to> method to trim the changes list down to the changes between the from and to indexes. It then loops over the changes, calling the C<verify_change> method for each change. If any errors occur, the method returns the number of errors. Otherwise, it returns 0.

The C<_trim_to> method is responsible for trimming the changes list down to the changes between the from and to indexes. It takes the changes list and the from and to identifiers as input, and returns a new list containing only the changes between the from and to indexes. If no from identifier is provided, the method returns the changes list as is. If no to identifier is provided, the method returns a list containing only the last change in the changes list.

