This function takes a $self object and a $key parameter, which is the ID or name of the change to seek. It first retrieves the changes object from the $self object and then uses the index_of method to find the index of the specified change in the changes list. If the change is not found, the function dies with a message indicating that it cannot find the change in the plan. If the change is found, the function sets the position of the iterator to the index of the change and returns the index.

Note that the function uses the _changes method to get the changes object from the $self object, which is a private method. The _position method is also used to set the position of the iterator.

